#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/albion.adoc:100
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/chaos.adoc:72
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[ogres,†1]]1. Ogres"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/albion.adoc:105
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/chaos.adoc:77
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/orcs.adoc:105
msgid ""
"If an Ogre unit can use its initiative to charge an enemy unit of humans at "
"the start of the Command phase then it must do so. This happens "
"automatically and their commander can do nothing about it. ‘Humans’ "
"encompasses all ‘men’ including Chaos Warriors and Marauders, but not "
"Dwarfs, Elves etc."
msgstr ""
"Si une unité d’ogres peut utiliser son initiative pour charger une unité "
"d’humains (littéralement humains… ce qui inclut les Guerriers et Maraudeurs "
"du Chaos, mais pas les Nains, les Elfes et autres humanoïdes) au début de la "
"phase d’Ordres, elle doit le faire, quels que soient les désirs de leur "
"commandant."

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/albion.adoc:106
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[giant,†2]]2. Giant"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/albion.adoc:109
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[giant-eagles,†3]]3. Giant Eagles"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/albion.adoc:110
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:95
msgid "Giant Eagles can fly."
msgstr "Les Aigles Géants peuvent voler."

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/albion.adoc:111
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[giant-eagle-mount,†4]]4. Giant Eagle Mount"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/albion.adoc:114
msgid ""
"Giant Eagles can be ridden only by Druids An Eagle can fly, increasing its "
"rider’s move from 60 to 100cm, and it adds +2 Attacks to those of its rider."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/albion.adoc:115
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[chariot-mount,†5]]5. Chariot Mount"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/albion.adoc:117
msgid ""
"Generals, Druids and Heroes can ride Chariots. An extra +1 Attack is added "
"to those of its rider."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/albion.adoc:118
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[fenbeast,†6]]6. Fenbeast"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/albion.adoc:122
msgid ""
"A Fenbeast is an individual troop unit, but it is not fielded in the "
"standard way. Fenbeasts appear on the battlefield only after a Druid casts "
"the Summon Fenbeast spell."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/albion.adoc:129
msgid ""
"A Fenbeast cannot be brigaded with other troop units, not even other "
"Fenbeasts. Fenbeasts never use their initiative to move in the Command "
"phase. Because they are completely dominated by the will of the Druid who "
"summoned them, that Druid counts as having a Command value of +1 when "
"commanding the Fenbeast – that is 8 rather than 7."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/albion.adoc:134
msgid ""
"Fenbeast can move through bogs as though they were open terrain. Unlike the "
"wild Bog Beasts from the ‘Dark Shadows’ campaign, Fenbeast will make way for "
"friendly troops."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/albion.adoc:136
msgid "A Fenbeast causes terror in its enemies."
msgstr ""

